.TH TRAFIX 1 "May 2026" "0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trafix \- Lightweight network monitoring tool for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trafix
.RI [ OPTION ]
.br
.B trafix interfaces
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B trafix connections
.RI [ --json ]
.RI [ "--proto tcp|udp" ]
.RI [ "--state STATE" ]
.br
.B trafix listeners
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B trafix system
.RI [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trafix is a lightweight terminal user interface and scriptable command-line tool that provides insights into Linux system, connection, and network activity.

Running
.B trafix
without options launches the interactive TUI.
Inside the TUI, help is available through a popup opened with
.BR F1 ,
.BR h ,
or
.BR H .
The popup lists the keys with short descriptions and closes with
.BR Esc ,
.BR Enter ,
or
.BR q .
The
.B x
key opens a process chooser and requests a kill after confirmation.
The
.B z
key opens a connection chooser and requests a drop where supported.
The
.B a
key shows the recent action audit in the support dock.
.br
The
.B g
key shows the troubleshooting diagnostics in the support dock.
.br
The
.B n
key shows the route and DNS checks in the support dock.
.br
The
.B v
key shows the network health correlation in the support dock.
.br
The
.B l
key opens the support dock selector.
The
.BR t
key toggles the top system, CPU, memory, and disk panels.
In the Network panel, the selected top talker can be moved with
.BR j
and
.BR k ,
and
.BR d
or
.BR Enter
shows the bandwidth detail in the support dock.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B interfaces
Print current network interface byte counters. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B connections
Print current TCP/UDP connections. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B listeners
Print local listening sockets. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B system
Print a compact system overview. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B diagnostics
Print a compact troubleshooting snapshot for network and system diagnosis.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display this help message and exit.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Use JSON output for scriptable commands.
.TP
.BI "--proto " tcp|udp
Filter
.B connections
output by protocol.
.TP
.BI "--state " STATE
Filter
.B connections
output by connection state, such as
.B ESTABLISHED
or
.BR LISTEN .
.TP
.B kill
Request a process kill from the CLI. The command requires a PID and accepts
.B --yes
to skip interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B drop
Request a connection or socket drop from the CLI. Supported forms are
.B drop connection
and
.B drop socket
with protocol and endpoints, plus
.B --yes
for non-interactive execution.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or general command failure.
.TP
.B 2
Required collector data is unavailable or permission-limited.
